  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Class 3 Notes",
      "start": 0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "These notes are a short to-do list from the third class, so let's go through it in order.",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5.08
        },
        {
          "text": "First on the list is making sense of the direct pathway.",
          "start": 5.36,
          "end": 9.08
        },
        {
          "text": "It got fifteen minutes of explanation, and barely any of it sank in.",
          "start": 9.28,
          "end": 13.52
        },
        {
          "text": "Next, a malfunction of the substantia nigra pars compacta means less dopamine, and that leads to Parkinson's disease.",
          "start": 14.08,
          "end": 21.8
        },
        {
          "text": "The indirect pathway needs the same work as the direct one.",
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 25.52
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps also read the book's chapter.",
          "start": 25.68,
          "end": 27.8
        },
        {
          "text": "Beyond that, the aim is to understand the mechanisms behind Parkinson's disease and Huntington's disease.",
          "start": 28.08,
          "end": 34
        },
        {
          "text": "As for the cerebellum, it belongs to the old brain.",
          "start": 34.24,
          "end": 37.48
        },
        {
          "text": "Then there are tremors, where the task is to tell active tremors apart from passive ones, and to know which kind is more present in which disease.",
          "start": 37.76,
          "end": 46.04
        },
        {
          "text": "You also need to know the mossy fibres and the climbing fibres.",
          "start": 46.24,
          "end": 49.92
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, when making notes on the cerebellum, focus on its functional divisions rather than its anatomy.",
          "start": 50.16,
          "end": 56.24
        },
        {
          "text": "And that's everything on the list for this class.",
          "start": 56.48,
          "end": 58.96
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
